WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:01.632 --> 00:05.168 align:center line:79%
If you've ever visited
our home state of Louisiana,

00:05.636 --> 00:11.508 align:center line:79%
you’re probably familiar with many of
our tasty dishes—gumbo, jambalaya,

00:11.742 --> 00:14.878 align:center line:81%
étouffée, and the list goes on and on.

00:15.345 --> 00:20.350 align:center line:79%
From time to time, I find myself
feeling bold enough to cook one

00:20.350 --> 00:22.019 align:center line:81%
of those tasty recipes.

00:22.986 --> 00:25.389 align:center line:81%
The undocumented final step

00:25.989 --> 00:31.795 align:center line:79%
after mixing all the ingredients
and following the detailed instructions

00:31.995 --> 00:36.433 align:center line:79%
is to do the final taste test
and see if anything is missing.

00:37.034 --> 00:43.106 align:center line:79%
At that point, I could hear the Creole
cooking legends whispering in my ears,

00:43.206 --> 00:45.275 align:center line:81%
“Put more Tony’s in it.”

00:45.909 --> 00:52.249 align:center line:79%
Tony’s is a Creole
seasoning made in Opelousas, Louisiana,

00:52.316 --> 00:59.356 align:center line:79%
my hometown. It's often used
as the secret ingredient to compensate

00:59.356 --> 01:03.193 align:center line:79%
for the imperfections made
while following the recipe.

01:05.429 --> 01:10.133 align:center line:79%
Michelle and I had the honor
to serve as mission leaders in Louisiana.

01:10.767 --> 01:14.137 align:center line:79%
We had a tradition of teaching
the missionaries how

01:14.137 --> 01:20.010 align:center line:79%
to cook her special jambalaya recipe
on their last night in the mission home

01:20.010 --> 01:21.979 align:center line:81%
before returning to their families.

01:22.613 --> 01:27.951 align:center line:79%
In addition to their testimonies
of the restored gospel of Jesus Christ,

01:28.518 --> 01:34.024 align:center line:79%
our missionaries left the mission
with an appreciation for recipes.

01:35.158 --> 01:40.030 align:center line:79%
A few months ago, I was browsing
through the Church media library

01:40.397 --> 01:47.571 align:center line:79%
and saw a link to a collection of short
videos called “Restoration Conversations

01:47.571 --> 01:50.140 align:center line:81%
with President Russell M. Nelson.”

01:50.707 --> 01:52.776 align:center line:81%
The title of one of those short videos

01:52.776 --> 01:56.346 align:center line:79%
in the list caught my attention
and made me smile.

01:56.813 --> 02:02.686 align:center line:79%
It was called “Scriptures Are God’s
Recipes for Happy Living.”

02:03.620 --> 02:06.556 align:center line:79%
I immediately clicked
on that two-minute video

02:06.923 --> 02:13.063 align:center line:79%
and watched President Nelson
teach a group of Primary kids a simple

02:13.063 --> 02:16.500 align:center line:79%
and powerful message
about how to be happy.

02:16.933 --> 02:22.539 align:center line:79%
He taught, “If you’re making a cake,
you follow the directions, don’t you?

02:23.240 --> 02:27.477 align:center line:79%
And you’ll get a good
result every time, won’t you?”

02:28.345 --> 02:33.050 align:center line:79%
He continued, speaking
about turning 95 years old soon:

02:33.383 --> 02:35.986 align:center line:81%
“People say, ’What do you eat?

02:36.253 --> 02:42.059 align:center line:79%
What’s your secret?’” He replied,
“The secret’s called the scriptures.

02:42.292 --> 02:45.629 align:center line:81%
You might read them and try them.”

02:46.029 --> 02:49.966 align:center line:81%
End quote. Well, there we have it.

02:49.966 --> 02:56.640 align:center line:79%
The simple secret for happy living is
to just follow God's recipe as detailed

02:56.640 --> 03:01.011 align:center line:79%
in the scriptures.
I call it the “Good News Recipe.”

03:02.379 --> 03:06.316 align:center line:79%
What do you do if something goes
wrong when following the recipe?

03:07.284 --> 03:08.518 align:center line:81%
We all—

03:12.255 --> 03:17.327 align:center line:79%
Well, embedded in the good news
recipe is the secret ingredient

03:17.327 --> 03:20.363 align:center line:79%
to ensure we always
get it right in the end.

03:20.964 --> 03:24.501 align:center line:81%
The answer is always Jesus Christ.

03:25.268 --> 03:29.840 align:center line:79%
I think we all have moments when we feel
our ingredients are not good enough,

03:30.640 --> 03:33.276 align:center line:81%
or we struggle to follow the directions.

03:33.810 --> 03:36.446 align:center line:81%
Or perhaps we do something out of order

03:37.047 --> 03:41.051 align:center line:79%
or something happens that's out
of our control, and so on.

03:41.885 --> 03:48.525 align:center line:79%
What's the remedy? It's simply
to add more of what invites Jesus Christ

03:48.525 --> 03:49.693 align:center line:81%
into your life.

03:50.761 --> 03:55.031 align:center line:79%
So what might it look like to add more
Jesus Christ in your life?

03:56.032 --> 03:58.034 align:center line:81%
While serving as mission president,

03:58.401 --> 04:01.772 align:center line:79%
I had the pleasure
of meeting personally with each

04:01.772 --> 04:07.210 align:center line:79%
of our young missionaries every six weeks.
During the one-on-one meeting,

04:07.410 --> 04:11.281 align:center line:79%
it was common for missionaries
to seek guidance on how

04:11.281 --> 04:15.018 align:center line:79%
to improve the effectiveness
of their companionships.

04:15.685 --> 04:20.757 align:center line:79%
On one occasion, a missionary came
into his personal interview and sat down.

04:21.658 --> 04:25.695 align:center line:79%
I could tell from his body language
that something was weighing heavily

04:25.695 --> 04:31.134 align:center line:79%
on his mind. I asked “Elder,
what would you like to discuss today?”

04:32.035 --> 04:36.206 align:center line:79%
He went on to describe some challenges
he was having with his companion,

04:36.640 --> 04:40.377 align:center line:79%
and how it was affecting their ability
to do missionary work.

04:41.311 --> 04:43.079 align:center line:81%
With tears in his eyes,

04:43.547 --> 04:45.315 align:center line:81%
he looked at me and asked,

04:45.649 --> 04:50.654 align:center line:79%
“President, what should I do?”
In that instance,

04:51.087 --> 04:53.723 align:center line:81%
I honestly didn't know how to respond.

04:54.758 --> 04:56.193 align:center line:81%
After a brief moment,

04:56.560 --> 05:00.897 align:center line:79%
I asked if it was okay
for us to kneel together in prayer

05:01.031 --> 05:02.732 align:center line:81%
for guidance from the Spirit.

05:03.166 --> 05:07.571 align:center line:79%
He agreed, and we knelt
together and prayed for inspiration.

05:08.438 --> 05:12.175 align:center line:79%
After the prayer, we continued
kneeling for a short time

05:12.809 --> 05:15.478 align:center line:79%
and then sat in our chairs
facing each other.

05:16.046 --> 05:21.151 align:center line:79%
I asked if we could read a scripture
together. As we opened our scriptures,

05:21.651 --> 05:26.890 align:center line:79%
I paused and told him,
“Elder, as we read this scripture,

05:27.524 --> 05:30.327 align:center line:79%
please ask yourself
the following question:

05:31.428 --> 05:33.797 align:center line:81%
If I live these attributes,

05:34.397 --> 05:39.636 align:center line:79%
will it improve my companionship
and our missionary work?”

05:40.437 --> 05:45.408 align:center line:79%
Then we opened Moroni
7:45 and read out loud.

05:46.776 --> 05:53.817 align:center line:79%
“And charity suffereth long and is kind,
and envieth not, and is not puffed up,

05:54.184 --> 06:00.123 align:center line:79%
seeketh not her own, is not
easily provoked, thinketh no evil,

06:00.223 --> 06:06.830 align:center line:79%
and rejoiceth not in iniquity, but
rejoiceth in the truth, beareth all

06:06.863 --> 06:12.769 align:center line:79%
things, believeth all things,
hopeth all things, endureth all things.”

06:13.336 --> 06:19.042 align:center line:79%
Then the elder looked at me with tears
in his eyes and said, “Yes, president,

06:19.409 --> 06:22.579 align:center line:81%
but that is hard to do.” I agreed

06:23.079 --> 06:28.752 align:center line:79%
and I reminded him that he is a son
of God with divine potential

06:28.752 --> 06:30.553 align:center line:81%
to do it together with the Lord.

06:31.354 --> 06:33.623 align:center line:81%
Then we briefly discussed the parable

06:33.623 --> 06:37.994 align:center line:79%
of the slope taught by
Elder Clark G. Gilbert of the Seventy,

06:38.261 --> 06:42.198 align:center line:79%
which reminded us that we need
to start where we are

06:42.832 --> 06:48.238 align:center line:79%
and, together with the Lord, move forward
and upward in a positive direction.

06:49.272 --> 06:54.110 align:center line:79%
I could tell he was still feeling
a bit overwhelmed about the next step,

06:54.945 --> 07:00.383 align:center line:79%
so I asked him to describe his
understanding of the scripture “by small

07:00.383 --> 07:03.820 align:center line:79%
and simple things are great
things brought to pass.”

07:04.621 --> 07:09.259 align:center line:79%
He went on to describe
the concept that by doing small

07:09.259 --> 07:11.795 align:center line:79%
and simple things,
great things could happen.

07:12.662 --> 07:16.700 align:center line:79%
I asked him to take a minute
and identify two small

07:16.700 --> 07:21.204 align:center line:79%
and simple things he could do
to be kind to his companion.

07:22.138 --> 07:25.008 align:center line:79%
After a few moments,
he shared his thoughts.

07:25.008 --> 07:30.180 align:center line:79%
Then I asked him to take a minute
and identify two small

07:30.180 --> 07:34.951 align:center line:79%
and simple things he could do
to be patient with his companion,

07:35.285 --> 07:37.887 align:center line:79%
he almost immediately
shared his two thoughts.

07:38.355 --> 07:42.092 align:center line:79%
It was clear he had already been pondering
this before our meeting.

07:42.993 --> 07:46.896 align:center line:79%
I invited him to take
those few items to God in prayer,

07:47.497 --> 07:49.599 align:center line:81%
and to ask for confirmation,

07:49.866 --> 07:56.740 align:center line:79%
direction, and inspiration on how
to execute his plan with real intent.

07:57.507 --> 08:00.310 align:center line:81%
He agreed. As we concluded,

08:00.577 --> 08:04.547 align:center line:79%
I asked him to provide a brief update
in his weekly letter.

08:05.348 --> 08:07.450 align:center line:81%
As the next few weeks went by,

08:07.851 --> 08:11.187 align:center line:79%
I could see in his weekly
letters that things were improving,

08:11.621 --> 08:15.658 align:center line:79%
but not only could I see the improvement
in his weekly letters,

08:15.992 --> 08:19.396 align:center line:79%
I could also see it in the weekly
letters of his companion.

08:20.296 --> 08:23.066 align:center line:81%
During our next in-person interview,

08:23.833 --> 08:27.170 align:center line:79%
I saw a night and day
difference in his confidence and spirit.

08:27.537 --> 08:32.275 align:center line:79%
I asked him, “So, elder,
is it true that charity never faileth?”

08:32.275 --> 08:34.978 align:center line:81%
He responded with a big smile,

08:35.211 --> 08:40.450 align:center line:79%
“Yes. And by small and simple
things are great things brought to pass.”

08:41.451 --> 08:45.221 align:center line:79%
As you follow the good news recipe
for happy living,

08:45.655 --> 08:48.058 align:center line:81%
remember President Nelson’s teaching:

08:48.625 --> 08:51.461 align:center line:81%
“Whatever questions or problems you have,

08:51.928 --> 08:57.033 align:center line:79%
the answer is always found in the life
and teachings of Jesus Christ.

08:57.434 --> 09:04.007 align:center line:79%
Learn more about His Atonement,
His love, His mercy, His doctrine,

09:04.174 --> 09:07.811 align:center line:79%
and His restored gospel
of healing and progression.

09:08.311 --> 09:10.947 align:center line:81%
Turn to Him! Follow Him!”

09:11.381 --> 09:14.951 align:center line:81%
End quote. When you need to hear Him

09:15.418 --> 09:18.655 align:center line:79%
and know how to invite
Jesus Christ into your life,

09:19.022 --> 09:23.093 align:center line:79%
consider following the steps
President Nelson taught us about

09:23.093 --> 09:25.862 align:center line:81%
personal revelation. Quote.

09:26.262 --> 09:29.299 align:center line:79%
“Find a quiet place
where you can regularly go.

09:29.966 --> 09:32.335 align:center line:81%
Humble yourself before God.

09:32.802 --> 09:35.572 align:center line:79%
Pour out your heart
to your Heavenly Father.

09:36.106 --> 09:38.842 align:center line:81%
Turn to Him for answers and for comfort.

09:39.142 --> 09:44.647 align:center line:79%
Pray in the name of Jesus Christ
about your concerns, your fears,

09:44.647 --> 09:48.985 align:center line:79%
your weaknesses. Yes,
the very longings of your heart.

09:49.619 --> 09:53.756 align:center line:79%
And then listen! Write the thoughts
that come to your mind.

09:54.324 --> 09:59.229 align:center line:79%
Record your feelings and follow through
with the actions that you are prompted

09:59.229 --> 10:04.901 align:center line:79%
to take. As you repeat this process,
day after day, month after month,

10:04.934 --> 10:09.439 align:center line:79%
year after year, you will grow
into the principle of revelation.”

10:09.739 --> 10:14.878 align:center line:79%
End quote. I testify that Jesus Christ
is our Savior and Redeemer.

10:15.278 --> 10:19.582 align:center line:79%
He has accomplished everything we need
to be able to return

10:19.582 --> 10:21.050 align:center line:81%
to our Heavenly Father.

10:21.217 --> 10:23.820 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

